 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbgADyos0ws/",
 "title": "Why you should never share your fragrance",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator advises that when someone asks about your fragrance or personal details, you should not explain everything. Keeping a sense of mystery builds curiosity and leaves a stronger, more confident impression.",
 "key_points": [
  "When someone says you smell good, never tell them what fragrance you are wearing.",
  "People with class understand that not everything valuable needs to be shared.",
  "The moment you explain every little detail, you remove curiosity, and curiosity is powerful.",
  "Instead of naming your fragrance, smile and say 'Thank you', 'I appreciate that', or 'I'm glad you like it'.",
  "If they ask again, say 'I'll let you wonder' or 'Some things are better left a mystery'.",
  "This applies to your entire life: you don't have to tell people where you shop, what your watch costs, how much money you make, or the secrets behind your success.",
  "The most unforgettable people reveal just enough to be remembered, but never enough to be predicted."
 ],
 "content": "When someone says you smell good never tell them what fragrance you're. It may seem like a simple question but sometimes the smallest answers leave the biggest impression. People with class understand that not everything valuable needs to be shared. Some things become part of your signature, your fragrance, your style, presence. The moment you explain every little detail you remove the curiosity and curiosity is powerful. So instead of instantly The name of your fragrance Simply smile and say thank you. I appreciate that. Or I'm glad you like it. If they ask again, don't feel pressured to answer. Just say I'll let you wonder. Or some things are better left a mystery. Notice what happens next. People become even more curious because confidence doesn't feel the explain everything. This isn't just about perfume. It's about your entire life. You don't have to Tell people Where you shop, what your watch cost, how much money you make or every secret behind your success. Leave people with something to wonder about. Remember, this is not everything that is valuable should be available. The most unforgettable people reveal just enough to be remembered but enough to be predicted. Instagram reel/post by YoungAdvisor_11. Text / caption: #young_artist #young_advisor It's not just about the perfume!",
